=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed existing widget patterns: LocationMapWidget, LocationFavoritesWidget, WidgetShell, WidgetMapView.
Checked Geofence type from @/types/location: id, name, latitude, longitude, radius, enabled, alertOnEntry, alertOnExit, costPerKwh, createdAt.
Checked useGeofences from @/api/hooks/useLocations — returns Geofence[] via /geofences.
Checked useVehicleState from @/api/hooks/useVehicles — returns state with latitude/longitude.
Checked useSettings for convertDistance + distanceUnit (radius in meters → user unit).
Confirmed Circle and Marker available from @/components/maps barrel.
Badge variants: info, success, warning, danger, neutral.

=== REASONING ===
Widget needs: geofence list with inside/outside status, compact mode showing current zone.
Haversine distance used to determine if vehicle is inside each geofence circle.
Radius stored in meters, converted via miles→user unit (meters/1609.344 = miles, then convertDistance).
Standard view (2×4): map with Circle overlays + scrollable fence list with badges.
Compact view (1×2): current zone name badge or "No zone".
WidgetMapView used for the map container, Circle from @/components/maps for geofence circles.
All strings via useTranslation('dashboard').
Null-safe: geofences ?? [], g.name ?? '—', g.radius ?? 0, g.enabled ?? true.
Freshness props passed to WidgetShell from both hooks (max of dataUpdatedAt).

